---
description: When trying to lint a typescript file. Applies to \*.ts, \*.tsx
alwaysApply: true
---

After completing a related batch of edits, run `yarn eslint --fix` on all changed
files together. Do not stop to lint after each individual file edit.

If you run into ESLint errors, try running `yarn eslint --fix` on the affected
files and then
re-reading the file: it could save manually fixing them.

If an ESLint error is caused by a debugging change, don't make any changes and
don't add a `//eslint-disable-next-line` comment. Just leave it as is. For
example:

```ts
// This fails `no-console`. Don't make any changes to this!
console.log('Debug log!');
```
